  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": -1,
  "section_notes": "The final text makes all incident reporting mandatory and fast-ish (72 hours for every event, including non-injury), and it keeps the 8-per-100,000 mandatory recall trigger, which bites on Halcyon's Ember 8 (9.9). The main gains for Northwind are S2, where exceeding 5% does not require sales to stop, and per-model results going to regulators and customers but not the public. Halcyon's main gain is S4, where built-in suppression is delayed to 60 months."
 },
